  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "Three animals that never forget your face.",
      "hold_after": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "crow1",
      "text": "First, crows. Scientists in Seattle caught some crows while wearing a scary mask."
    },
    {
      "id": "crow2",
      "text": "For years afterwards, the crows screamed at anyone wearing that mask."
    },
    {
      "id": "crow3",
      "text": "Even crows that were never caught joined in, and they taught their chicks to do it too."
    },
    {
      "id": "sheep1",
      "text": "Next, sheep. Scientists at Cambridge taught sheep to recognize celebrities, like Barack Obama and Emma Watson, just from photos."
    },
    {
      "id": "sheep2",
      "text": "They got it right about eight times out of ten."
    },
    {
      "id": "bee1",
      "text": "Finally, honeybees. Bees can learn to recognize a human face in a photo, and still remember it two days later."
    },
    {
      "id": "bee2",
      "text": "With a brain smaller than a grain of rice."
    }
  ]
